CHANGELOG – php-demo / BPA-Demo
================================

All changes are listed in reverse chronological order.
Format: YYYY-MM-DD @ HH:MM  <summary>

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-07-09 @ 17:05 - [Fix - agent health dashboard panels all rendered empty]:
  User reported all panels on "BPA-Demo * Agent Health" (added 16:10 today)
  were empty. Root cause: `dx-do metric data`'s `agentExpression` regime
  strips the `SuperDomain|` prefix before matching (the 3-segment
  bare-path regime used for the earlier alert/SLI verification work in
  this project), but the dashboard's own NASS query engine
  (`basicFilters[].sourceNameSpecifier[].pattern`) matches the FULL
  `metric.source` string, which always starts with `SuperDomain|`. Every
  `sourceNameSpecifier` pattern in the dashboard template was written in
  the bare 3-segment form -- correctly verified against `metric data`
  before shipping, which is exactly why the bug wasn't caught: that
  verification used a different API surface than the one the dashboard
  actually queries, and `metric data` silently normalizes away the exact
  prefix the dashboard needs. Same underlying "3-/4-segment path regime"
  confusion as the bpa-demo-management-module.sh agentExpressions bug
  from 2026-07-06 and documented under reference-agent-expressions, just
  hitting a third API surface (NASS dashboard queries) this time.
  Found via the empirical-discovery move from the dx-done-nas skill:
  probed the raw `dx-do nass query` API directly with a minimal
  FROM_METADATA + KEEP payload. The bare-path pattern returned zero
  rows; the identical pattern with `SuperDomain\|` prepended returned
  the real metric -- confirmed for all 13 sourceNameSpecifier patterns
  in the template (3 polystat traffic lights + 10 metric-graph targets),
  not just the one that first exposed the bug.
  Fixed by prepending `SuperDomain\|` to every sourceNameSpecifier
  pattern in dxo2-scripts/templates/bpa-demo-agent-health-dashboard.json.
  Re-verified all 18 panels' query patterns individually against the raw
  `nass query` API before redeploying via
  `bpa-demo-agent-health-dashboard.sh create` (upserted in place, same
  uid, no duplicate). Confirmed via a fresh `dashboard-export` that the
  live tenant copy carries the fix, not just the local template.
  Lesson recorded in CLAUDE.md and dxo2-scripts/README.md: `dx-do metric
  data` is not a valid stand-in for verifying a dashboard's own NASS
  query shape -- use `dx-do nass query` (or `dashboard-render`, which
  this dx-do build doesn't have) to verify dashboard `sourceNameSpecifier`
  patterns specifically.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-07-09 @ 16:10 - [Feat - dxo2-scripts/bpa-demo-agent-health-dashboard.sh: agent status dashboard]:
  Added "BPA-Demo · Agent Health" dashboard to the pre-existing "BPA-Demo"
  dashboard folder (found a folder and a dashboard,
  "BPA-Demo PHP Probe · Overview", already there from earlier work,
  neither created by any tracked script -- left both untouched and added
  this as a complementary, agent-scoped overview).
  Three sections: an "Agent Status" row of 3 grafana-polystat-panel
  traffic-light circles (Infrastructure Agent, PHP Probe Agent, BPA
  WebServer Agent), then each agent's basic metrics (Infra: DB
  Availability/Connection Refusals/Cache Hit Rate/Slow Query Rate; PHP:
  App Response Time/Error Rate/Concurrency/DB Backend Response Time;
  Browser: Page Load Time/Page Hits).
  Each traffic light queries the reserved "Custom Metric Agent (Virtual)"
  alert-status metric (Alerts|BPA-Demo:<alert name>, published by the EM
  for every alert on an active Management Module -- confirmed via
  `dx-do metric data`, a discrete 0=no-data/1=ok/2=warning/3=critical
  severity scale) with a regex matching every alert belonging to that
  agent's tier, rolled up to the WORST severity among them via a
  polystat composite (globalOperatorName: "max") -- green only if every
  alert for that agent is currently OK. Reuses the alerts
  bpa-demo-management-module.sh/bpa-demo-agent-alerts.sh already
  created; no new alert.
  Verified live before wiring anything in, not guessed: every
  alert-status regex and every metric-graph pattern was checked against
  real `metric data` output first, including confirming the lights show
  a genuine mix of severities (values 1/2/3 across different alerts) --
  at verification time the PHP Probe Agent light was legitimately red
  from a leftover elevated error-rate alert from earlier fault-injection
  testing (see the 14:35 entry above), not a dashboard bug.
  This dx-do build's `dashboard` command group turned out to be missing
  dashboard-create, dashboard-delete, validate-layout, and
  dashboard-render entirely -- a smaller surface than some dx-do
  documentation describes for newer builds. Adapted:
  (1) dashboard-export/import/update all take dashboardExportFile=, not
  dashboardFile= as documented.
  (2) dashboard-import's preserveUid=true overwrite=true upsert doesn't
  work here -- overwrite= is silently ignored (request body always
  shows "overwrite":false), which omits the version field Grafana
  requires and fails with HTTP 412 version-mismatch.
  (3) dashboard-update does NOT resolve a numeric id from a bare uid on
  this build either (fails "Export dashboard does not have an id!" even
  with uid set) -- contrary to some documentation for newer builds. The
  classic export -> edit -> update workflow (real numeric id +
  meta.folderId from a fresh export, splice in the regenerated panels,
  push back via dashboard-update) is what actually works, and is what
  `create`'s self-heal path does.
  (4) No dashboard-delete exists at all -- `delete` prints manual
  console-removal instructions instead of pretending a CLI command
  exists.
  (5) No dashboard-render exists either, so no PNG self-check was
  possible; verification relied on dashboard-export/check (panel
  count/types/titles) plus the live metric data checks above, and
  hand-checked 24-column grid geometry (no local validate-layout
  available to lint it).
  Verified idempotent: re-ran create twice, confirmed dashboard-search
  shows exactly one dashboard (uid unchanged, version incremented 1->2),
  and confirmed check still reports all 18 panels correctly both times.
  New: dxo2-scripts/bpa-demo-agent-health-dashboard.sh (create/check/
  delete, same convention as every other script in this directory),
  dxo2-scripts/templates/bpa-demo-agent-health-dashboard.json (the
  dashboard JSON).
  dxo2-scripts/README.md, CLAUDE.md: documented the dashboard and every
  landmine found on this dx-do build.

