2026-07-09 @ 14:35 - [Docs - Situations never form from BPA-Demo's alarms, investigated and documented]:
  User asked to create "situation alarms" for the existing alarms/metrics.
  Found dx-do situation has no create command -- Situations are entirely
  auto-correlated by DX O2's AIOps engine from firing alarms, not a
  user-defined resource like Alerts/SLIs.
  Verified live whether the existing alerts (bpa-demo-management-module.sh,
  bpa-demo-agent-alerts.sh) actually feed that correlation, in two rounds:
  (1) triggered the trouble use case for real (sustained curl traffic as
  the trouble user); confirmed 4 alerts fired within ~30s of each other,
  all on the same entity (bpa-demo-php-probe) -- Trouble User High
  Response Time, PHP Probe App Response Time High, PHP Probe DB Backend
  Query Storm, PHP Probe App Error Rate Rising. situation query stayed
  [] for ~15 minutes.
  (2) to rule out same-entity-only correlation, stopped the mariadb
  container for ~2 minutes (docker stop/start, no volumes touched) to
  force a genuine cross-tier fault -- confirmed via dxo2 sidecar logs
  (SQLNonTransientConnectionException/UnknownHostException: mariadb)
  and app behavior (/shop returned 500 throughout, /health stayed 200
  as designed) that both tiers broke simultaneously. Confirmed two
  distinct-CI alarms fired within ~90s of each other: Infra Agent - DB
  Availability Down (Infrastructure Agent CI) and Trouble User/PHP
  Probe App Response Time High (PHP probe agent CI). Polled
  situation query every 30s for a full 10 minutes after restoring
  mariadb. Still [] throughout.
  Conclusion: a genuine two-tier incident still produced zero
  Situations across ~25 minutes of combined testing -- ruled out
  same-entity-only correlation as the cause. No fix identified from the
  CLI alone; needs the console's own Situations view checked directly
  or confirmation from Broadcom on what enables correlation for a
  tenant this size. Demo stack confirmed fully healthy after both test
  rounds -- no lasting side effects.
  BUGS: new entry with full reproduction detail. CLAUDE.md: cross-
  referenced from bpa-demo-agent-alerts.sh's paragraph.

