2026-07-08 @ 18:10 - [Feat - traffic-generator: anonymous traffic, concurrency, pacing shaping]:
  User reported response-time averages in DX O2 looking suspiciously flat
  when run on the same host. Root cause: the generator ran exactly one
  session at a time, strictly sequentially -- zero real request overlap,
  so there was never any genuine server-side contention to produce
  natural variance in measured response times.
  Added three independent changes to traffic-generator/generator.py:
  (1) TRAFFIC_ANONYMOUS_RATIO (default 0.8): each cycle now builds a
  shuffled mix of exactly one authenticated session per demo user plus
  enough anonymous guest sessions (new run_guest_session(), no login at
  all) to reach this ratio of the cycle's total -- 14 users -> 56 guest
  sessions -> 70 total at the default 80/20 split, matching how most
  real e-commerce traffic is anonymous browsing. Guest sessions run the
  identical weighted action set including checkout, since checkout.php's
  order_create() already accepts a null user id (guest checkout) -- no
  app changes needed. The one-authenticated-session-per-user guarantee
  is unaffected, so trouble/empty_basket/locked still fire every cycle
  regardless of this ratio. Extracted the shared action loop into
  _run_session_actions() so both session kinds pick actions the same way.
  (2) TRAFFIC_CONCURRENT_SESSIONS (default 3): a small pool of worker
  threads (stdlib threading + queue.Queue, no new dependencies) now
  pulls from each cycle's shuffled session list and runs sessions in
  parallel instead of one at a time -- this is the mechanism that
  actually produces response-time variance, via genuine request overlap
  and real contention (Apache workers, MariaDB connections).
  (3) TRAFFIC_SLOWDOWN_PROBABILITY/_MIN_SECS/_MAX_SECS (defaults
  0.12/3/12): new sleep_with_shaping() layers an extra randomized delay
  on top of normal per-action pacing this fraction of the time, widening
  the pacing distribution beyond a narrow uniform range and increasing
  the odds of concurrent workers' requests landing close together.
  Verified live end to end, not just read: rebuilt the image, watched
  the generator's own logs confirm the exact 70-session/14-authenticated/
  56-anonymous split and multiple sessions genuinely overlapping in time
  (one session's full lifecycle straddling two others'), confirmed
  Apache's access log showing multiple distinct requests landing within
  the same second, confirmed a guest checkout completing end to end
  (order created with no prior login), and confirmed the slowdown branch
  fires via a temporary high-probability debug run.
  docker-compose.yml, build-scripts/compose.sh, .config.example: wired
  the three new TRAFFIC_* variables through with the same defaults.
  traffic-generator/README.md, CLAUDE.md: documented the new behavior.

