2026-07-08 @ 16:55 - [Fix - order confirmation X-Page-ID metric-path explosion]:
  User reported the Business Payload Analyzer creating one metric path per
  checkout. Root cause: app/src/pages/order.php's confirmation view passed
  the numeric order ID as the set_monitoring_headers() target
  (ORDER-CONFIRM-186, ORDER-CONFIRM-187, ...) -- BPA groups business
  transactions by the full X-Page-ID, so every completed checkout ever
  since launch had accumulated its own distinct metric path.
  Fixed to a fixed 'SUCCESS' target (ORDER-CONFIRM-SUCCESS for every
  order), mirroring the sibling order-not-found case's existing fixed
  'NOTFOUND' target on the same page. Checked all other
  set_monitoring_headers() call sites (basket/shop/login/admin/product/
  checkout) -- none of the others pass a numeric or otherwise unbounded
  value, so this was the only offender.
  Verified live end to end, not just read: rebuilt the apache-php image,
  logged in as a demo user via curl, completed two separate real
  checkouts (order ids 225 and 226), and confirmed both produced the
  identical X-Page-ID: ORDER-CONFIRM-SUCCESS header; also confirmed the
  sibling ORDER-VIEW-NOTFOUND path is unaffected.
  CLAUDE.md: documented the X-Page-ID cardinality rule (fixed string or
  small bounded set only, never a numeric row ID) so future pages don't
  reintroduce this.

