2026-07-07 @ 17:45 - [Fix - dxo2-scripts/bpa-demo-sli.sh: tenant user email no longer hardcoded]:
  The SLI import payload's createdBy/created_by attribution was hardcoded
  to the tenant user who wrote it (JOERG.MERTIN@BROADCOM.COM) -- a problem
  for anyone else running this against their own tenant, since that login
  is specific to one person and may not exist elsewhere. Replaced all 3
  occurrences in dxo2-scripts/templates/bpa-demo-response-time-sli.json
  with a __DXO2_TENANT_USER_EMAIL__ placeholder. Added
  DXO2_TENANT_USER_EMAIL to .config/.config.example (new "DX O2 tenant
  configuration scripts" section). bpa-demo-sli.sh: new load_config()
  (sources .config, fatals if DXO2_TENANT_USER_EMAIL is unset) and
  render_template() (sed-substitutes the placeholder into a mktemp'd
  file, cleaned up with rm -f right after the import call) -- only
  cmd_create needs either; check/delete are unaffected and still work
  without a .config present. Verified: substitution produces valid JSON
  with zero placeholders remaining, and check/create's idempotent no-op
  path (the SLI already exists from the prior commit) both still work
  unchanged.
  CLAUDE.md, dxo2-scripts/README.md: documented the mechanism.

