2026-07-07 @ 10:00 - [Fix - o2-universe console crash-on-edit; dx-do upgraded to v6.4.0]:
  Upgraded tools/dx-do-linux-x64 from v6.3.5 to v6.4.0 (downloaded from the
  public github.com/kialambroca/dx-do-dist mirror, with explicit
  confirmation, after the canonical internal
  github.gwd.broadcom.net/IMS/dx-do-mono release host was unreachable
  without a VPN tunnel and, once tunneled, required a GHE credential this
  session doesn't have). Confirmed the release notes' Authorization-header
  leak fix (the same bug found and worked around while writing
  bpa-demo-service.sh) is real: the same error path that used to dump a
  live Bearer token to stdout no longer does. Old binary kept alongside as
  dx-do-linux-x64.v6.3.5.bak. Confirmed the new "agentic mcp" experimental
  mode (a stdio MCP server for AI agent clients) is not applicable to
  dxo2-scripts/ -- those scripts must run standalone for a human with no
  AI in the loop, which is incompatible with an MCP server that expects an
  MCP client to drive it; no changes made on that basis.
  Investigated a user-reported console crash editing the "BPA Demo
  universe" O2 Universe (VIEW617, created by
  bpa-demo-services-universe.sh's original `o2-universe create` call).
  Diffed it against a Universe the user created manually through the
  console's own wizard (VIEW618, label "BPA Demo", scoped to the existing
  "BPA-Demo" Service). Root cause confirmed identical to the earlier
  404-on-open finding in dxo2-scripts/dx-do-o2-universe-issue.md: CLI
  creation via `o2-universe create` always leaves the Universe unscoped
  (tas view filter {"op": "ALL"}, nass view serviceFilter.values: []),
