  recreate): (1) `[[ -f "${STATE_FILE}" ]] && source "${STATE_FILE}"` as a
  function's LAST statement dies under `set -e` when the file doesn't
  exist -- the common first-run case -- because the function's own return
  status becomes the compound statement's (nonzero) exit code; fixed with
  an explicit `if` guard in both bpa-demo-agent-alerts.sh's and
  bpa-demo-management-module.sh's load_state(). (2) `declare -p` output
  sourced from inside a function creates a *local* (not global) array by
  bash's default scoping rule, so idempotency silently broke (every
  create call saw empty state and tried to recreate everything); fixed by
  forcing `declare -gA` on the sourced state file's array declarations.
