2026-07-02 @ 11:00 - [Fix – DB Monitor "SELECT command denied" for performance_schema]:
  src/dx-o2-agents/entrypoint.sh: _ensure_monitor_user() now re-applies the
  GRANT SELECT, PROCESS, REPLICATION CLIENT ON *.* every start regardless of
  whether the login already existed, not only on first creation.  Root cause:
  MariaDB's own MARIADB_USER bootstrapping already creates phpuser, scoped
  only to grants on its own database (phpapp.*); the DB Monitor extension
  then failed with "SELECT command denied to user 'phpuser'@'...' for table
  performance_schema.global_variables" because the pre-existing login never
  received the global grant.  CREATE USER IF NOT EXISTS remains a no-op
  (including the password clause) when the login is already present, so an
  existing password is never overwritten -- only the GRANT is reapplied.
  CLAUDE.md: updated the login-verification description to reflect that
  grants are (re-)applied unconditionally, not only for newly created logins.
  Verified: docker exec into mariadb confirms `SHOW GRANTS FOR 'phpuser'@'%'`
  now includes SELECT, PROCESS, BINLOG MONITOR (MariaDB's name for
  REPLICATION CLIENT) ON *.*, and the "SELECT command denied" error no longer
  appears in dxo2 logs after a restart.

