2026-07-01 @ 09:00 - [Fix – PHP probe logLevel written as string instead of number]:
  src/apache-php/entrypoint.sh: added name-to-number mapping (case statement)
  before writing wily_php_agent.logLevel.  The INI only accepts numeric values
  (0=trace,1=debug,2=info,3=warning,4=error,5=fatal); the entrypoint was writing
  the raw APMIA_PHP_LOG_LEVEL string (e.g. "INFO") which the probe ignores,
  leaving the INI default.  Now maps TRACE/DEBUG/INFO/WARN*/WARNING/ERROR/FATAL
  and their numeric equivalents; falls back to 2 (INFO) for unknown values.
  Also removed quotes around the numeric value in the INI (the probe expects an
  unquoted integer).  Log output now shows level=INFO/2.
  .config.example: updated comment to document the 0-5 scale.
  CLAUDE.md, COMPATIBILITY.md, DX-O2-AGENT-SETUP.md: updated to reflect that
  logLevel is numeric and that name-to-number mapping is performed at startup.
