2026-06-20 @ 01:00 - [Fix – APMIA and BTListener logs empty in dxo2 status page (Kubernetes)]:
  Root cause: dx-o2-agent had no volumeMounts in the Helm deployment
  template.  The IA wrote IntroscopeAgent.log and BTListener.log to the
  container's private overlay filesystem.  apache-php mounts apmia-share
  (seeded once by dxo2-init) and reads /opt/apmia/logs/ from there –
  a static copy with no live log files, so all log cards were empty.
  In Docker Compose both services mount apmia_data read-write/read-only
  at /opt/apmia; the same volume makes logs visible.  Kubernetes lacked
  this shared mount on the dx-o2-agent side.
  Fix: added volumeMount for apmia-share at /opt/apmia in the dx-o2-agent
  container spec (deployment.yaml).  The IA now writes to apmia-share,
  which apache-php reads via its existing read-only mount – identical to
  the Compose behaviour.  Docker Compose is unchanged.
  File: helm/php-demo/templates/deployment.yaml

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-06-20 @ 00:30 - [Fix – dx-o2-agent logs not visible in kubectl logs / docker compose logs]:
  The IA (IntroscopeAgent.log) and BTL (BTListener.log) write to files
  rather than stdout.  kubectl logs and docker compose logs only capture
  stdout/stderr, so neither log was visible.
  Fix: added _await_and_tail() helper to src/dx-o2-agents/entrypoint.sh.
  After starting each daemon, a background tailer waits up to 60 s for
  the log file to appear (JVM start-up delay), then exec's tail -F to
  stream it to stdout indefinitely.  Two tailers are started:
  - BTListener.log: inside the BTL else block (only when BTL is present)
  - IntroscopeAgent.log: unconditionally after the BTL block
  IA_TAIL_PID and BTL_TAIL_PID are tracked and killed in _shutdown() so
  the tailers stop cleanly on SIGTERM/SIGINT.
  Works identically in Kubernetes (kubectl logs) and Docker Compose
  (docker compose logs) -- no Helm or Compose changes required.

