2026-06-19 @ 23:15 - [Fix – Kubernetes liveness/readiness probes return HTTP 500 with APMIA enabled]:
  Root cause: probes hit GET / → index.php → APMIA PHP probe extension
  tries TCP connect to 127.0.0.1:5005 (IA collector) → sidecar not ready
  yet → 500.  Fix: add a static health file (app/src/health) served by
  Apache without invoking PHP, so probes never trigger the extension.
  Changes:
  - app/src/health: new static file ("OK"), no PHP extension so mod_php
    is not invoked; Apache serves it via the default file handler.
  - src/apache-php/config/vhost.conf: added SetEnvIf to suppress access
    log entries for /health probe requests; updated CustomLog with
    env=!dontlog to exclude flagged requests from log output.
  - helm/php-demo/values.yaml: changed probe paths from / to /health for
    livenessProbe and readinessProbe; added startupProbe (30 × 5 s =
    150 s startup window) so liveness does not fire during slow starts.
  - helm/php-demo/templates/deployment.yaml: added {{- with startupProbe }}
    block so the new startupProbe key from values.yaml is rendered.
  - CLAUDE.md: documented static health endpoint in Helm chart section.

