2026-06-18 @ 20:00 - [Fix – ASCII-only entrypoints; BTListener.sh start argument]:
  Two issues found when running the dx-o2-agents entrypoint interactively:

  1. BTListener.sh printed its usage line and exited immediately because it
     was called without an argument.  BTListener.sh requires an explicit 'start'
     argument to daemonize the Java process.  The entrypoint now calls
     "${BTL_SCRIPT}" start (no background '&' needed as start handles that).

  2. Both entrypoint.sh files contained non-ASCII characters used as section
     separators: U+2500 box-drawing (─), U+2013 en dash (–), U+2192 arrow (→).
     These can cause byte-sequence errors in strict locale environments and make
     the files harder to grep or process with standard POSIX tools.

  Both files were fully rewritten replacing all separators with plain ASCII:
    # ── Title ─────  →  # == Title ===
    –                →  -
    →                →  ->

  Verified: grep -Pc '[^\x00-\x7F]' returns 0 on both files.

  Files changed:
  - src/dx-o2-agents/entrypoint.sh: BTListener.sh start; ASCII-only separators.
  - src/apache-php/entrypoint.sh: ASCII-only separators (no functional change).

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-06-18 @ 15:30 - [Fix – dxo2.php: probe INI glob detection; BPA via apache2ctl]:
  Two detection methods in app/src/pages/dxo2.php were incorrect.

  PHP probe INI detection:
  - Previous: hardcoded /etc/php/8.1/apache2/conf.d/wily_php_agent.ini.
  - Actual layout: the real INI file lives in mods-available/ and is symlinked
    into conf.d/ as 99-wily_php_agent.ini.  The entrypoint may produce any
    numeric prefix (99-, etc.) so exact-name matching is fragile.
  - Fix: glob $phpConfD . '/*-wily_php_agent.ini' (where phpConfD is built from
    PHP_MAJOR_VERSION / PHP_MINOR_VERSION at runtime), take the first match, and
    resolve its real path with realpath() to display both the symlink and the
    actual mods-available target.

  BPA module detection:
  - Previous: parsed /etc/apache2/conf-enabled/bpa.conf for the LoadModule name,
    then checked apache_get_modules() for that derived name.
  - Actual: the BPA Apache module always registers internally as caplugin_module
    regardless of the filename.  apache_get_modules() (mod_php SAPI) may not
    reflect modules loaded outside the main httpd.conf; apache2ctl DUMP_MODULES
    is authoritative.
  - Fix: shell_exec('apache2ctl -t -D DUMP_MODULES 2>&1'), parse lines matching
    /^\s+(\w+_module)\b/, search for caplugin_module specifically.  Falls back
    to apache_get_modules() if shell_exec is unavailable.  Raw DUMP_MODULES
    output displayed verbatim in a scrollable block.

  File changed: app/src/pages/dxo2.php

