      6.1 Infrastructure Agent + BTL entrypoint flow (envsubst → APMIAgent →
          btl → signal trap → wait)
      6.2 PHP Probe injection (wily_php_agent.ini guard → copy .so → symlink
          .ini → run install helper)
      6.3 BPA WebServer Plugin injection (ngx_http_ca_plugin_filter_module.so
          guard → write load_module to modules-enabled/bpa.conf → copy
          webserver_plugin.ini → nginx -t validates)
      6.4 Complete Kubernetes pod startup sequence diagram (initContainers →
          parallel container start with volume mount annotations)
  - Section 7: Configuring the agent — .config variables, profile rendering
    table (envsubst substitutions), TLS EM (port 5443, SSLSocketFactory) guide.
  - Section 8: Verification — kubectl logs expected output for all three
    containers, curl header check (X-Page-ID), kubectl exec php -m / nginx -T
    extension checks, EM connectivity test.
  - Section 9: Troubleshooting — five named problems with symptoms, root cause,
    and fix commands:
      "Probe files not found" (dxo2-init failure)
      "unknown directive load_module" (missing top-level include)
      "module is not binary compatible" (NGINX version mismatch)
      "PHP probe loads but no data" (EM unreachable)
      "BTL binary not found" (embedded BTL in newer APMIA — not an error)
      Docker Compose: optional apmia_data volume recipe for local testing.
  - Section 10: End-to-end checklist (12 items, check-box format).

