2026-06-15 @ 17:15 - [Phase 4 – Build System Hardening & DX O2 Pipeline Integration]:
  Rewrote all build-scripts/ shell scripts to OpenWaterFoundation Shell Best
  Practices (OWF), wired the DX O2 agents image into the push/deploy pipeline,
  and extended .config.example with DX O2 and Helm configuration variables.

  Task 4.1 – build.sh (OWF rewrite):
  - Full function-based structure: usage(), info(), fatal(),
    check_prerequisites(), load_config(), compute_build_tag(), build_image(),
    package_app(), cleanup().
  - check_prerequisites() verifies docker binary and live daemon (docker info).
  - load_config() sources .config and validates REGISTRY, IMAGE_PREFIX,
    IMAGE_TAG, and BUILD_PLATFORM with ${:?} parameter expansion; fatal on
    any missing variable.
  - compute_build_tag() increments .build_number, strips any existing b<N>
    suffix from IMAGE_TAG, derives FULL_TAG, persists it back to .config via
    sed, and re-sources the file so the current shell is in sync.
  - build_image() centralises docker build invocation: --platform, --pull,
    --no-cache flags; human-readable label in log output.
  - Step 4 (dx-o2-agents) is skipped gracefully with an informative message
    when no apmia-*.tar.gz installer is found; builds 1–3 are unaffected.
  - New --push flag: invokes push.sh automatically after a successful build.
  - All variables that should not be rebound are declared readonly; all
    function-local variables are declared with local [-r].

  Task 4.2 – package-app.sh (OWF rewrite):
  - Function-based: usage(), info(), fatal(), check_prerequisites(),
    load_config(), create_archive().
  - check_prerequisites() validates the tar binary.
  - create_archive() validates app/src/ exists before archiving; reports
    output archive path and size.
  - Adds -h/--help flag.

  Task 4.3 – push.sh (OWF rewrite):
  - Function-based: usage(), info(), fatal(), check_prerequisites(),
    load_config(), registry_login(), push_image(), registry_logout().
  - load_config() validates REGISTRY, REGISTRY_USER, REGISTRY_PASSWORD,
    IMAGE_PREFIX, IMAGE_TAG.
  - registry_login() uses `printf '%s' | docker login --password-stdin`
    to avoid passing credentials on the command line.
  - push_image() checks local image existence via docker image inspect before
    pushing; emits a clear warning (not a fatal error) when an image is
    absent so a partial push does not abort the remaining images.
  - registry_logout() clears stored credentials from the Docker credential
    store after all pushes complete.
  - New --skip-dxo2 flag: skips the dx-o2-agents push (e.g. when the
    installer was absent during build and the image was not produced).
  - Adds -h/--help flag.

  Task 4.4 – deploy.sh (OWF rewrite):
  - Function-based: usage(), info(), fatal(), check_prerequisites(),
    load_config(), resolve_chart_path(), generate_values(), ensure_namespace(),
    run_deploy(), post_deploy_init().
  - check_prerequisites() validates helm and kubectl binaries; verifies cluster
    reachability via `kubectl cluster-info`.
  - load_config() validates all 14 required deployment variables.
  - resolve_chart_path() honours HELM_CHART_PATH from .config (falls back to
    helm/php-demo); fatal if the directory does not exist.
  - generate_values() emits a transient values.local.yaml with:
      image.dxo2.repository / .tag (new – covers dx-o2-agents image)
